WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.130
In the driest parts of the Atacama,
measurable rain may fall only once every 5

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.210
to 20 years.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:12.790
Beneath the Salar de Atacama, a
salt flat about 2,300 metres up,

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.370
lies brine rich in lithium.

5
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.330
Batteries account for 88 per
cent of world lithium use.

6
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.130
In 2025, Chile produced an
estimated 56,000 tonnes,

7
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.010
of about 290,000 worldwide.

8
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.530
So who decides who pumps it?

9
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.290
Whoever buys the land above?

10
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.970
The communities alone?

11
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.010
In this mission, you'll weigh the
salar's opportunities and challenges,

12
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.690
from strong sun to scarce water.

13
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.730
Then you'll map the stakeholders, from
companies to Atacameño communities,

14
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.450
and judge a water dispute.

15
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.110
Your mission: find out who decides
who pumps the Atacama's lithium.
